    <briefdescription>
<para>Vulkan device context published to the phonebook by the OpenXR session owner (oxr_interface) for use by other plugins. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>On Android + OpenXR the Vulkan device is created by the OpenXR runtime (via xrCreateVulkanDeviceKHR / XR_KHR_vulkan_enable2) and is not accessible through any other <ref refid="namespaceILLIXR" kindref="compound">ILLIXR</ref> service. oxr_interface registers an instance of this struct after <ref refid="namespaceILLIXR_1a519c5fa22ffb9588a1c96607155f1ea0" kindref="member">create_session()</ref> completes; any plugin that needs a VkDevice can call <ref refid="classILLIXR_1_1phonebook_1a3d292059ea83e59808695622fec36fe2" kindref="member">phonebook::lookup_impl&lt;vulkan_device_context&gt;()</ref> without any direct dependency on oxr_interface.</para>
<para>The handles are owned by oxr_interface for the lifetime of the XrSession; consumers must not destroy them. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
